Magicbane is not fairly charactized by hit damage per round.  It
also scares, purges and sometimes confuses victims.  In order to
use the simple hit damage per round measure you have to consider
Magicbane's _average_ hit damage per round (which is somewhat
higher than the numbers you've presented).  Still, this doesn't
tell the whole story since a stunned or scared victim may not
fight back and a purged victim will be unable to use its magic
attack.  In those cases, you are, in effect, getting a free round
of damage.  With those considerations in mind, you are correct in
noting that Magicbane does indeed fare poorly by the simple hit
damage per round criteria.  It is not a barbarian-style weapon.
Also, a confused victim might actually wander off and seemingly
attack other monsters for you!

